---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="How Sovereign Stack curates listings, what the jurisdiction fields mean, and the advertising policy."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">About</h1>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What this is</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-stone-600">
      Sovereign Stack is a curated directory of technology you can actually
      own: open-source software, self-hostable platforms, independently-domiciled
      services, and open hardware. We catalog products from the EU, the US, and
      the rest of the world — because digital sovereignty is not one country's
      project.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Methodology</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-stone-600">
      Every listing records the facts a sovereignty-minded buyer needs:
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-stone-600">
      <li><strong class="text-stone-900">Company domicile</strong> — the legal jurisdiction of the vendor, as an ISO country code.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-stone-900">Data residency</strong> — where customer data can physically reside.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-stone-900">License</strong> — SPDX identifier, or Proprietary.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-stone-900">Self-hosting</strong> — whether you can run it on your own infrastructure.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-stone-900">What it replaces</strong> — the incumbent product, so migrations are discoverable.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3 text-stone-600">
      Listings are editorial and free. Inclusion is not for sale.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Advertising policy</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-stone-600">
      The directory is free to browse and free to be listed in. Revenue comes
      from clearly labeled sponsorships: featured placements, category
      sponsorships, and sponsored guides. Paid placement never changes editorial
      rankings, and every paid slot is labeled as sponsored. Rankings are
      editorial; visibility is for sale. That line is the product.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">AI access</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-stone-600">
      Every listing is published as clean semantic HTML with structured data,
      plus a machine-readable JSON feed at <a href="/api/listings.json" class="underline">/api/listings.json</a>
      and a summary at <a href="/llms.txt" class="underline">/llms.txt</a> for AI assistants and agents.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
